        "baud_rate": 115200,
        "comments": "-> [[docs:techref:hardware:port.serial]] general information about the serial port, serial port cable, etc.\n\nHow to connect to the Serial Port of this specific device:\n\n| {{media:doc:hardware:serial:usb_to_rs232.ttl.jpeg?100|}} | Use a [[docs:techref:hardware:port.serial#usb.to.rs232.ttl.converter.module|serial TTL]] adapter to connect your PC with the router. Only connect TX, RX and GND. |\n  **Settings:**\\\\\n  * Baudrate: 115200\n  * Data bits: 8\n  * Parity: None\n  * Stop bits: 1\n\nThe serial port is located at the Jumper J2 on the board:\\\\ {{media:netgear:dgnd3800:dgnd3800b_serial.jpg?400|}}\n\n<a2s>\n 11       9       7       5       3       1\n#--------------------------------------------#\n|.-.     .-.     .-.     .-.     .-.     .-. |\n|'-'     '-'     '-'     '-'     '-'     '-' |\n+--------------------------------------------+\n|.-.     .-.     .-.     .-.     .-.     .-. |\n|'-'GND  '-'TX   '-'     '-'     '-'RX   '-' |\n#--------------------------------------------#  J2\n 12      10       8       6       4       2\n</a2s>\n\nIf you're using an [[https://www.adafruit.com/product/954|RPi Prolific adapter]]; connect black to GND, White to TX and Green to RX\n\nSerial flashing how-to: [[http://www.richud.com/wiki/DGND3700_V1_CFE_Boot_Loader_TFTP_De-Brick|External Link]]\n",
